Subject: Expose where an environment's page-number lists start

Adds one function, mdbx_r_env_heap_roots(), which reports the malloc() start
of the two page-number lists (`wr.repnl`, `wr.retired_pages`) owned by an
environment's preallocated write transaction. It reads two pointer fields and
calls nothing.

libmdbx keeps a page-number list by a pointer one element past the start of
its block (pnl_alloc() returns `pnl + 1`). That is fine while the environment
is closed in time, which frees the lists. But this package deliberately never
closes two kinds of environment: one that has panicked, which must not
re-enter libmdbx, and one inherited across a fork(), which belongs to the
parent. Both stay allocated until the process exits, and valgrind, finding
only interior pointers to their lists, reports every one as "possibly lost".
CRAN runs valgrind with its default --errors-for-leak-kinds=definite,possible,
so each became an error in the log: after 0.1.2 fixed everything else, these
were the only errors left that came from this package -- 8 loss records in
each of 27 forked test children, and more in the main test process.

The package records the start addresses after each open and each write
transaction, beside the handle and in its registry of abandoned handles, and
never dereferences them. The function is for valgrind's sake only. It changes
nothing in libmdbx: no existing line is touched.

Rejected alternative: --leak-check-heuristics. None of valgrind's heuristics
matches a 4-byte offset (length64 is for 8), and CRAN does not set them.

--- a/src/vendor/libmdbx/mdbx.c
+++ b/src/vendor/libmdbx/mdbx.c
@@ -42807,3 +42807,20 @@
     __attribute__((__externally_visible__))
 #endif
     const char *const mdbx_sourcery_anchor = sourcery;
+
+/* R package patch: the start addresses of the two page-number lists an
+ * environment's preallocated write transaction owns, or null. Reads two
+ * pointer fields and nothing else; the package records the result next to
+ * environments it may never close, so that valgrind can see those lists are
+ * still owned. See tools/patches. */
+void mdbx_r_env_heap_roots(const MDBX_env *env, void *roots[2]);
+void mdbx_r_env_heap_roots(const MDBX_env *env, void *roots[2]) {
+  roots[0] = roots[1] = nullptr;
+  if (env == nullptr || env->basal_txn == nullptr)
+    return;
+  const MDBX_txn *const txn = env->basal_txn;
+  if (txn->wr.repnl)
+    roots[0] = txn->wr.repnl - 1;
+  if (txn->wr.retired_pages)
+    roots[1] = txn->wr.retired_pages - 1;
+}
